# Golden files are compared byte for byte, and a checkout that rewrites line endings makes
# every one of them fail on that machine alone. Git for Windows turns `core.autocrlf` on by
# default, and the GitHub Windows runners keep it on, so the working tree is pinned to LF
# here rather than left to each machine's configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exception, and it has to come last to win: this file carries the carriage return a
# checkout on Windows leaves behind, and it is the fixture that proves rune trims it. Any
# line-ending conversion, in either direction, would delete the defect the test exists to
# catch.
crates/rune-cli/tests/fixtures/version-crlf.txt -text
